   "kotoba-lang/standard-model#3 merged as 9689fb877a961611a44d171b6614e45ca2f9c163:
    Phase 0b -- position gauge field h_mu (4x4 real matrix, row mu = physical
    four-vector h_mu) and derived metric g_munu=h_mu.h_nu via kotoba.sm.tensor/dot
    unmodified; flat-limit check is EXACT integer equality against
    kotoba.sm.tensor/metric, not epsilon-close; consistency with pre-existing
    global SO(3,1)+ (kotoba.sm.vector-field boosts/rotations) proven algebraically
    (Lambda^T eta Lambda=eta => Lambda eta Lambda^T=eta) and checked against 7
    concrete transformations. No general matrix inverse implemented (deferred)."
   "kotoba-lang/standard-model#4 merged as cc10dcb6a571451f20a5f328b7ca9d7aff0d8d62:
    test-only edge-case coverage hardening (generator antisymmetry, field-strength
    antisymmetry, covariant-derivative linearity, diagonal-Gram guards,
    derived-metric symmetry) that SURFACED A REAL BUG: kotoba.sm.gauge/field-strength's
    self-interaction term g*f^abc*A_mu^b*A_nu^c is antisymmetric under mu<->nu only
    when excited gauge-field components share the same trace-Gram sign -- true
    automatically for compact SU(2)/SU(3) (uniform K=1/2) but false for so(1,3)'s
    mixed boost(-1)/rotation(+1) components. Recorded honestly as a passing test
    documenting current (broken) behavior per this repo's practice, not silently
    patched; fix filed as separate follow-up rather than rushed inline."
   "kotoba-lang/standard-model#5 merged as 9e94650961ef1792a46c77a3fb8bc307b29f64db:
    Phase 0c -- curvature-quadratic-invariant, I = sum_k K[k][k]*(R_munu^k R^munu_k),
    built from Phase 0a's R_munu alone, scoped to h=position-gauge-identity only
    (the one case needing no matrix inverse). Explicitly documented as NOT the LDG
    curvature scalar R=h^mu^h^nu.R(hbar_nu,hbar_mu) (that is LINEAR in R_munu; this
    is QUADRATIC, same relationship Kretschmann scalar has to Riemann tensor in GR).
    Implementing agent declined to guess at the true linear contraction's index-
    pairing convention without an independent literature value to check against --
    filed as named follow-up (Phase 0d) rather than risking a silently-wrong result.
    Not guaranteed non-negative (K is indefinite)."
   "independent adversarial review (a dedicated task, no code changed, not itself a
    PR): re-derived so(1,3) commutation relations, Gram-matrix signs (boost=-1,
    rotation=+1, verified by hand from Dirac-representation gamma matrices), and the
    generalized structure-constant formula from Peskin&Schroeder BEFORE reading the
    implementation, then checked for divergence -- found existing algebra correct,
    but identified the EXACT root cause of PR #4's antisymmetry bug: self-interaction-term
    indexed structure-constants as f-abc[a][b][c] (output index FIRST) where
    structure-constants' own definition [T_A,T_B]=if^ABD*T_D puts the output/target
    index THIRD; verified the fix (swap to f-abc[b][c][a]) three independent ways
    (re-indexed reimplementation, direct matrix ground truth via -ig[A_0,A_1],
    bit-identical SU(2) regression) before any production code touched"
   "kotoba-lang/standard-model#6 merged as 6ed2ca0d9a881d8a8126328001dabb2bc394ff2a:
    implements exactly the review's diagnosed fix (get-in f-abc [a b cc] ->
    [b cc a]); SU(2)/SU(3) proven bit-identical via independent-oracle regression
